// Weighing the question below: convenience argues for the row, drift argues for the ladder, and only drift is a
// correctness argument.
data ledger_sighting_cannot_state_what_it_established: IntegrationConcern = IntegrationConcern {
  identity: "ledger_sighting_cannot_state_what_it_established",
  kind: SuspectedCapabilityGap {
    model: decl_field_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode", decl_name: "RecurringFailureMode", field_name: "receipts"),
    requirement: "a row states, per sighting, what that sighting established -- that a build did not stop, as distinct from a behaviour or a resolving route being observed -- so that a claim can refuse a read rung whose sightings are all of the weaker kind, without the claim being handed its own grade by its caller",
    standing: RequirementUnestablished {
      decided_by: "a claim over the ledger that refuses a row reporting a read rung while every one of its sightings is of the weaker basis, and that accepts the same row once a sighting of the stronger basis is present, and that downgrades no row merely because its evidence list is empty: at main 12253b17b3ae 95 of the 227 rows reporting a read rung carry evidence: [] legitimately, since the ledger header has evidence witness the class through computed references while receipts carry the prose the authored fold consumes, so a grade derived from the evidence field fails this requirement. It is unestablished today because the grade can only be supplied by the test: the closed guard #16671 shows the shape, its two claims passed and neither could fail on anything the ledger said.",
    },
  },
  affected: FreeSemigroup {
    head: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode", decl_name: "RecurringFailureMode"),
    tail: [
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode", decl_name: "RungReading"),
      decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_argument", decl_name: "guarantee_ladder"),
    ],
  },
  question: "Where does the ledger record what a sighting established, so that a claim can refuse a rung bought with a weaker sighting than the rung requires -- on the row, or in the guarantee ladder that already states what establishes a rung? The row placement is convenient and creates two statements about one fact; the ladder placement keeps one authority and re-derives every standing.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: sighting_basis_guard_revision,
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode", decl_name: "RecurringFailureMode") },
        tail: [
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.bare_name_resolved_only_by_the_flat_namespace", decl_name: "bare_name_resolved_only_by_the_flat_namespace") },
          CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.design_argument", decl_name: "guarantee_ladder") },
        ],
      },
      account: "Filed by still-otter-809 on 2026-11-18 while closing the loop on the first observed-to-compile specimen recorded on bare_name_resolved_only_by_the_flat_namespace (gunb-ai/gunbc#16667), whose W7 receipt already admits this geometry: a bare type-position name in an import-bearing file compiled and executed under the v1 path, and the resolving route was never established. The caveat that a guard would have to enforce exists only as prose in that receipt, because no field or sum can carry it. The guard that tried to enforce it (#16671 at 0fd8ac6e0ed2d8e277a5d1f477e14dfabf25991a) passed its claims and was still closed, on the ground that its basis was test-supplied. Measurement of the 95-of-227 read-rung rows with empty evidence was taken at main 12253b17b3ae7a38fa331531a422efc727f5761b by counting rows whose declaration reports a read rung against rows whose evidence list is empty, over every row file under dag/gunbc/recurring_failure_mode excluding the roster.",
